tion of your reasoning.\n        """\n        reasoning_type = await self.generate(instruction=analysis_instruction, context=self.problem_text)\n\n        # Step 3: Generate candidate answers using parallel approaches\n        candidate_answers = await asyncio.gather(\n            self.generate(\n                instruction=f"""\n                Given the reasoning type: {reasoning_type}\n                Use the extracted information: {extracted_info}\n                Solve the problem step by step, ensuring all logical connections are made.\n                Provide the final answer as a concise text span.\n                """,\n                context=self.problem_text\n            ),\n            self.generate(\n                instruction=f"""\n                Given the reasoning type: {reasoning_type}\n                Use the extracted information: {extracted_info}\n                Solve the problem using an alternative approach.\n                Ensure the reasoning is distinct from the first method.\n                Provide the final answer as a concise text span.\n                """,\n                context=self.problem_text\n            )\n        )\n\n        # Step 4: Ensemble to select the best answer\n        ensemble_instruction = f"""\n        Evaluate the following candidate answers:\n        - Candidate 1: {candidate_answers[0]}\n        - Candidate 2: {candidate_answers[1]}\n        Select the best answer based on accuracy, completeness, and adherence to the reasoning type.\n        If both are equally valid, provide a merged or synthesized version.\n        """\n        final_answer = await self.ensemble(instruction=ensemble_instruction, contexts=candidate_answers)\n\n        return final_answer\n```', '<think>\n</think>\n\n</think>\n\n```python\n# --- DO NOT IMPORT HERE ---\nclass Workflow:\n    def __init__(self, config, problem) -> None:\n        # --- DO NOT MODIFY THIS SECTION ---\n        self.config = config\n        self.problem_text = pr